1
00:00:00,225 --> 00:00:05,335
(Q11（单选）) Welcome to Manham Port, where a thousand years of history are brought to life.

2
00:00:05,335 --> 00:00:27,506
All the family can enjoy a day out at Manham: visit our copper mine, see models of the machinery it used, have your photo taken in nineteenth-century costume, experience at first hand how people lived at different stages throughout history, and especially how children studied, worked and played.

3
00:00:27,506 --> 00:00:43,030
[Q11干扰项C： 只是描述位置， 并不是C中说的good 位置， 偷换概念] The port of Manham is located in beautiful and peaceful countryside, on a bend in the great River Avon, and developed here because it's the highest navigable point of the Avon - boats can go no higher up this river&nbsp;

4
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:51,159
[Q11答案句（B） handy = convenient， load and unload = transport 解释型] and proved a handy place to load and unload cargo to and from the sea, which is over 23 miles away.&nbsp;

5
00:00:51,159 --> 00:01:10,411
(Q12) [Q12答案句（B）：tremendous need ... develop，   need = demand， develop=increase] A small port was already established here when, about 900 years ago, tin was discovered nearby, though it wasn't until the Industrial Revolution, when a tremendous need for metals of all kinds developed, that Manham expanded to become one of the busiest ports in the country.

6
00:01:10,411 --> 00:01:24,046
And because it was already so busy, prospectors began to look for other minerals, and by the end of the nineteenth century, lead, copper, manganese and arsenic were added to the cargos leaving Manham.

7
00:01:24,046 --> 00:01:31,554
(Q13) In the early days, the ores had been smelted - or processed - in the same area they were mined.

8
00:01:31,554 --> 00:01:47,948
[Q13答案句] But, as demand grew, the smelting process required huge factory furnaces or fires to melt the metal from the rock and there was not enough coal in the local area, so the rocks containing minerals had to be shipped Iong distances.

9
00:01:47,948 --> 00:01:56,938
(Q14) [Q14答案句（A）emigrate = went away] Sadly, in the twentieth century, the great port of Manham declined, and thousands of workers were forced to emigrate out of the area.

10
00:01:56,938 --> 00:02:02,843
The building at the port fell into disrepair, and the place became almost forgotten.

11
00:02:02,843 --> 00:02:08,646
(Q15) But then, the Manham Trust was formed to conserve the historical resources of the area.

12
00:02:08,646 --> 00:02:16,699
[Q15干扰项A、B：  【A】发现的是 original outline，而不是 original port的地点。 【B】召集志愿者 不等于 给 失业unemployed提供工作] It organised scores of local volunteers to remove undergrowth to find the original outlines of the installations.

13
00:02:16,699 --> 00:02:26,810
[Q15答案句（C）] It then brought in paid professionals to match installations with maps of the original port complex and to set about reconstructing it.

14
00:02:26,810 --> 00:02:32,115
Today you can see the results of this ambitious programme of restoration.

15
00:02:32,115 --> 00:02:45,203
The intention, and we believe this will be realised before the end of the year, is to return Manham Port to the condition it reached at its peak as 'the greatest copper port in the country'.

16
00:02:45,203 --> 00:02:48,550
(Q16（Table填空）) [铜矿参观体验] But what can you do and see on your visit today?

17
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:54,553
Here are just a few highlights. We suggest you start with the visit to the copper mine.

18
00:02:54,553 --> 00:03:03,580
Travel on converted mining trains and journey into the depths of the mountain along seams once worked by hundreds of miners.

19
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:08,886
Watch out especially for the great pumping machines which rid the mine of water.

20
00:03:08,886 --> 00:03:21,546
But please be warned that, like all mines, ours is very dark and closed in and we do say that children under five and also dogs should NOT be taken into the mine.

21
00:03:21,546 --> 00:03:25,748
[村庄学校与游戏展览] The next recommended visit is to the village school.

22
00:03:25,748 --> 00:03:32,707
While looking round the classrooms, take a special look at our display of games, which is one of the largest in the world.

23
00:03:32,707 --> 00:03:37,839
And it's recommended that you time your visit to coincide with a guided tour.

24
00:03:37,839 --> 00:03:42,060
This will give you the opportunity to ask lots of questions.

25
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:47,333
[古老帆船与参观提醒] Near the school is the beautiful old sailing ketch called The George'.

26
00:03:47,333 --> 00:03:50,961
You are welcome to board the boat and look round the cabins.

27
00:03:50,961 --> 00:03:58,528
Look out for the ship's wheel which was missing until only five years ago when it was dredged out of the silt by a local fisherman.

28
00:03:58,528 --> 00:04:05,528
We have no idea how it got there but it's been polished and proudly restored to its original place on the boat.

29
00:04:05,528 --> 00:04:13,077
Please take care going down the ladders if you wish to visit the lower deck - we don't recommend you allow young children to use them.

30
00:04:13,077 --> 00:04:15,577
So we hope you have a memorable visit to Manham Port and will tell your friends all about us.

